          {
            "id": "reveal-31",
            "category": "meaning",
            "severity": "minor",
            "detail": "«В его руке оказывается» makes the bouquet sound as if it suddenly appears. The source says Trench turns to reveal a bouquet he is already holding; rephrase to preserve that action.",
            "resolved": false,
            "source_anchor": {
              "quote": "Trench turns to reveal a bouquet of red roses held in his hand.",
              "occurrence": 0
            },
            "translation_anchor": {
              "quote": "Тренч оборачивается, и в его руке оказывается букет красных роз.",
              "occurrence": 0
            },
            "resolves": null
          },
          {
            "id": "attend-44",
            "category": "meaning",
            "severity": "minor",
            "detail": "“Went to” says they attended the same university; «поступили» specifically says they entered or were admitted. Use a rendering such as «учились в одном и том же женском университете».",
            "resolved": false,
            "source_anchor": {
              "quote": "Yeah, I think they actually went to the same all-women’s university.",
              "occurrence": 0
            },
            "translation_anchor": {
              "quote": "Да, кажется, они даже поступили в один и тот же женский университет",
              "occurrence": 0
            },
            "resolves": null
          },
          {
            "id": "flow-41",
            "category": "style",
            "severity": "minor",
            "detail": "«Разговор течёт так гладко» is an awkward calque in Russian. Prefer a natural equivalent such as «разговор идёт так легко» while preserving the sense of ease.",
            "resolved": false,
            "source_anchor": {
              "quote": "The conversation flows so smoothly; it’s so easy to spill his heart out to Zachariah, to reveal so much about his past, the good, the bad, and even the ugly.",
              "occurrence": 0
            },
            "translation_anchor": {
              "quote": "Разговор течёт так гладко; так легко излить душу Захарии, рассказать так много о своём прошлом — о хорошем, плохом и даже неприглядном.",
              "occurrence": 0
            },
            "resolves": null
          },
          {
            "id": "haunts-49",
            "category": "meaning",
            "severity": "minor",
            "detail": "“Old haunts” refers to familiar places he used to frequent, not necessarily places he considers favorites. «Любимые» adds an unsupported judgment; use a more neutral rendering.",
            "resolved": false,
            "source_anchor": {
              "quote": "I could show you all my old haunts.",
              "occurrence": 0
            },
            "translation_anchor": {
              "quote": "Я мог бы показать тебе все свои старые любимые места.",
              "occurrence": 0
            },
            "resolves": null
          },
          {
            "id": "obliges-56",
            "category": "register",
            "severity": "minor",
            "detail": "«Подчиняется» makes Darling sound as though he is submitting or obeying. “Obliges” here means he willingly complies with the request; choose a lighter equivalent.",
            "resolved": false,
            "source_anchor": {
              "quote": "Grinning, Darling obliges.",
              "occurrence": 0
            },
            "translation_anchor": {
              "quote": "Улыбаясь, Дарлинг подчиняется.",
              "occurrence": 0
            },
